THIRD PARTY CREDITS AND NOTICE

Farm Vendor is a new Lua program. Its workflow (a remembered sell list built
from your inventory, then select and sell each stack) comes from these
RedGuides macros. No code was copied from either one. Their authors keep all
rights in their original works; the MIT license above covers Farm Vendor's
own code only and grants nothing in those works.

  Sellitem.mac                                 Cannonballdex
    https://www.redguides.com/community/resources/authors/cannonballdex.233812/
  AutoVendor 3.6 (AutoVendor.mac)              Ionis
    https://www.redguides.com/community/resources/autovendor.1930/
    https://www.redguides.com/community/threads/autovendor.75143/

What came from which work is listed in README.md, "Credits", and on the
CREDITS line of every Lua file.
